## 3.0 Medical Plan Options\
\
Innovatech Solutions offers four medical plan options through **WellnessCorp**, our healthcare partner. All plans include preventive care at 100% (in-network) and cover essential health benefits as required by the Affordable Care Act (ACA).\
\
### 3.1 Plan Comparison (Plan Year 2024)\
\
| Feature | PPO Gold | PPO Silver | HMO Standard | HDHP (High Deductible) |\
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\
| **Plan Type** | PPO (Preferred Provider) | PPO | HMO | HDHP |\
| **Network** | National PPO | National PPO | Regional HMO | National PPO |\
| **Primary Care Visit** | $20 copay | $30 copay | $15 copay | Deductible, then 20% |\
| **Specialist Visit** | $40 copay | $50 copay | $30 copay | Deductible, then 20% |\
| **Emergency Room** | $250 copay | $350 copay | $300 copay | Deductible, then 20% |\
| **Urgent Care** | $40 copay | $50 copay | $40 copay | Deductible, then 20% |\
| **Inpatient Hospital** | $500 copay + 20% | $750 copay + 30% | $500 copay + 20% | Deductible, then 20% |\
| **Outpatient Surgery** | $200 copay + 20% | $300 copay + 30% | $200 copay + 20% | Deductible, then 20% |\
| **Preventive Care** | 100% covered | 100% covered | 100% covered | 100% covered |\
| **Mental Health / Substance Abuse** | $20 copay | $30 copay | $15 copay | Deductible, then 20% |\
| **Maternity Care** | 100% covered | 100% covered | 100% covered | Deductible, then 20% |\
| **Prescription Drugs** | See Section 5.0 | See Section 5.0 | See Section 5.0 | See Section 5.0 |\
| **Annual Deductible (Individual)** | $500 | $1,000 | $500 | $3,000 |\
| **Annual Deductible (Family)** | $1,000 | $2,000 | $1,000 | $6,000 |\
| **Out-of-Pocket Maximum (Individual)** | $3,000 | $4,500 | $3,000 | $6,000 |\
| **Out-of-Pocket Maximum (Family)** | $6,000 | $9,000 | $6,000 | $12,000 |\
| **HSA Eligible** | No | No | No | Yes |\
| **Referral Required** | No | No | Yes (for specialists) | No |\
| **Out-of-Network Coverage** | Yes (higher cost) | Yes (higher cost) | No | Yes (higher cost) |\
\
### 3.2 Plan Descriptions\
\
#### 3.2.1 PPO Gold\
- **Best for:** Employees who want predictable copays, low deductibles, and the flexibility to see any provider without a referral.\
- **Network:** National PPO network with access to over 1 million providers.\
- **Out-of-Network:** Covered at 60% after deductible (higher out-of-pocket costs apply).\
- **Ideal for:** Families with frequent medical needs or those who travel frequently.\
\
#### 3.2.2 PPO Silver\
- **Best for:** Employees who want moderate premiums with moderate out-of-pocket costs.\
- **Network:** Same national PPO network as Gold.\
- **Out-of-Network:** Covered at 50% after deductible.\
- **Ideal for:** Employees who are generally healthy but want flexibility and a lower premium.\
\
#### 3.2.3 HMO Standard\
- **Best for:** Employees who want the lowest premiums and are comfortable using a defined network of providers.\
- **Network:** Regional HMO network (available in CA, NY, IL, TX, FL, WA, and CO).\
- **Referral Required:** Yes, for all specialist visits.\
- **Out-of-Network:** Not covered (except emergencies).\
- **Ideal for:** Employees who live in a service area and want predictable, low-cost care.\
\
#### 3.2.4 HDHP (High Deductible Health Plan)\
- **Best for:** Employees who want the lowest premiums, are generally healthy, and want to save for future medical expenses through an HSA.\
- **Network:** National PPO network.\
- **Out-of-Network:** Covered at 60% after deductible.\
- **HSA:** Eligible for a Health Savings Account with a company contribution of $500 annually.\
- **Ideal for:** Employees who want to maximize tax-advantaged savings and are comfortable with higher deductibles.\
\
