## 6.0 Prescription Drug Coverage\
\
Prescription drug coverage is included with all medical plans and is administered by **RxPlus**.\
\
### 6.1 Prescription Tiers\
\
| Tier | Drug Type | PPO Gold | PPO Silver | HMO Standard | HDHP |\
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\
| **Tier 1** | Generic | $10 copay | $15 copay | $10 copay | Deductible, then $10 |\
| **Tier 2** | Preferred Brand | $30 copay | $40 copay | $30 copay | Deductible, then $30 |\
| **Tier 3** | Non-Preferred Brand | $60 copay | $75 copay | $60 copay | Deductible, then $60 |\
| **Tier 4** | Specialty | 20% coinsurance (max $200) | 30% coinsurance (max $250) | 20% coinsurance (max $200) | Deductible, then 20% (max $200) |\
\
### 6.2 Prescription Notes\
- **Mail Order:** 90-day supplies are available for Tier 1 and Tier 2 medications at 2x the retail copay.\
- **Prior Authorization:** Certain medications require prior authorization. Your doctor must submit a request to RxPlus.\
- **Step Therapy:** Some medications require you to try a lower-tier alternative first.\
- **Preventive Drugs:** Certain preventive medications (e.g., statins, contraceptives) are covered at 100% as required by the ACA.\
